title: "Style Genericide: Simulation Code and Outputs"
version: v1.0-run1
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DGK-Law-and-Cognition-Lab/Fair-Use-Style-Genericide-Computational"
# This DOI covers all versions and always points to the newest release.
# Each release also has a DOI of its own, listed in README.md.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24184659
abstract: >-
  A simulation of how AI imitation can wear away the link between artists and
  their styles ("style genericide"), and which legal rules keep that link.
  Twelve artists, one AI company and buyers meet in a small art market under
  seven legal regimes: no AI, fair use, opt-out, three licensing rules, and
  crediting the artist. The artists and the AI company learn by trial and
  error and then settle on choices that none of them can improve alone. The
  repository holds the code, every saved table and figure, checksums, and
  checks that rebuild the outputs byte for byte. This release is Run 1, second
  version, of 5 November 2026, in which every setting is assumed, not
  measured. It supports the Article "Style Genericide" by David G. Kamper.
authors:
  - given-names: "David G."
    family-names: Kamper
    affiliation: "University of Chicago Law School; Department of Psychology, University of California, Los Angeles"
keywords:
  - copyright
  - fair use
  - generative AI
  - artistic style
  - agent-based model
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - sensitivity analysis
